{
  "$defs": {
    "A2aBlock": {
      "description": "Agent-to-agent switchboard settings (nested under 'config.agents.a2a').\n\nGoverns the stream-json session-to-session switchboard (epic,\nGroup 2). `auto` is the A2A toggle: when true (the default), a switchboard\n`send A->B` runs the bounded literal-injection relay (B's reply becomes a\nuser turn in A, A's reply relays back to B, ...) up to `turn_ceiling` total\nturns, then stops with a visible \"loop ceiling reached\". When false it falls\nback to OBSERVED mode: B is driven once and its reply is mirrored into A's\nview, with no autonomous relay.\n\n`turn_ceiling` is a HARD correctness bound (a runaway A<->B exchange burns\nplan credit); it applies regardless of `auto` and must be >= 1.",
      "properties": {
        "auto": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Auto",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "turn_ceiling": {
          "default": 6,
          "title": "Turn Ceiling",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "title": "A2aBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AccountsBlock": {
      "description": "Account rotation and provider configuration (nested under 'config.accounts').",
      "properties": {
        "active": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Active"
        },
        "active_combo": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Active Combo"
        },
        "auto_switch": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Auto Switch",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "combos": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/ComboBlock"
          },
          "title": "Combos",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "failover": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/FailoverBlock"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "quota": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/QuotaBlock"
        },
        "records": {
          "items": {
            "additionalProperties": true,
            "type": "object"
          },
          "title": "Records",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "title": "AccountsBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ActiveBacklogConfig": {
      "description": "Active backlog dispatcher settings (nested under 'config.active_backlog').\n\nThe opt-in for the always-on backlog drain daemon (node): when\nenabled for a project, the per-user supervisor daemon continuously claims\nready backlog nodes for that project and dispatches them one at a time\nthrough the existing megawalk loop primitive, sleeping between drains with\nan event nudge for low latency.\n\nDefault OFF (footnote convention): a disabled block is byte-for-byte\ntoday's behavior. The fail-safe posture mirrors ``config.auto_continue`` /\n``config.target.blast``: a malformed block degrades to disabled rather than\nraising out of the whole settings load, a bad scalar field is dropped to its\ndefault (never raised), and an invalid ``interval`` (zero, negative, or\nunparseable) disables the feature rather than spinning a 0-sleep hot loop\n(Boundaries).\n\nFields\n------\nenabled:\n    ``True`` to drain every project, or a per-project map\n    ``{<project>: bool}`` to scope the daemon to specific projects.\n    Default ``False``. A scalar typo fails safe to disabled; in a map, only\n    a clear affirmative (``true``/``yes``/``on``/``1``) enables a project.\ninterval:\n    Poll-floor cadence as a duration string (``\"5m\"``, ``\"30s\"``, ``\"2h\"``,\n    ``\"1d\"``) or a bare integer (seconds). Default ``\"5m\"``. The poll floor\n    is the correctness guarantee; the event nudge is a latency optimization\n    layered on top.\nfailure_limit:\n    Consecutive dispatch failures before a node is parked (the circuit\n    breaker). Default 3. Reset to zero only on a successful close.\nmax_concurrent:\n    GLOBAL ceiling on concurrent converge runs (``backlog advance --epic``)\n    across every mission, never per mission. Default 1 (serial).\nmission: IGNORED (missions are per-epic graph state, never config; ``fno config doctor`` warns when it is set; the live axis is ``fno backlog advance --epic <id>`` / ``--stop``).",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            {
              "additionalProperties": {
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              "type": "object"
            }
          ],
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enabled"
        },
        "failure_limit": {
          "default": 3,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Failure Limit",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "interval": {
          "default": "5m",
          "title": "Interval",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "max_concurrent": {
          "default": 1,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Max Concurrent",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "mission": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Mission"
        }
      },
      "title": "ActiveBacklogConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AgentBeatBlock": {
      "description": "`config.agents.<harness>.beat`; `auto` reads the harness capability row.",
      "properties": {
        "beat": {
          "default": "auto",
          "title": "Beat",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "title": "AgentBeatBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AgentProviderBlock": {
      "description": "Per-provider agent-runtime settings (nested under 'config.agents.<provider>').\n\n`headless_yolo` (redefined by the bounded-posture amendment)\nselects FULL yolo vs the BOUNDED posture for an autonomous (headless,\nMODE==exec) codex/gemini worker. Both postures never prompt (no hang); they\ndiffer on the sandbox:\n\n  - False (default) -> BOUNDED: sandboxed AND never-prompt. codex\n    `--sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval never`; gemini\n    `--approval-mode yolo --sandbox`. No hang, and the worker cannot roam\n    outside the workspace.\n  - True -> FULL YOLO: unsandboxed bypass. codex\n    `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`; gemini bare `--yolo`. The\n    explicit opt-in for an operator who genuinely wants no sandbox.\n\nThe default is False (bounded) because it kills the headless hang WITHOUT\ndropping the sandbox - strictly safer than the full bypass. A malformed\nblock fails safe to bounded. Only the autonomous exec lane consults it; an\ninteractive `host`/`drive` launch and claude (yolo is a no-op) are never\naffected.",
      "properties": {
        "headless_yolo": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Headless Yolo",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "AgentProviderBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AgentsBlock": {
      "description": "Agent-runtime settings (nested under 'config.agents').\n\n`confirm` is always, auto (skip only resolved caveat-free node builds), or never. The default is auto; invalid values fail the read and callers degrade toward confirmation.",
