      },
      "title": "AgentsBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ApprovalsBlock": {
      "description": "Who may approve a consequential effect (nested under 'config.approvals').\n\nThis is the independent policy source the approval store consults at decision\ntime and again at execution time. It lives in config, not in a role manifest\nor a plugin declaration, precisely so that no runtime object can add itself\nto the authorized set: a role may declare an authority ceiling but cannot\ngrant one, and a transport carries a decision without minting its semantics.\n\nMaps an effect class to the principal ids allowed to decide it. The key `*`\nmatches every class, which is the solo-founder shape. Absent or empty means\nNOBODY may approve: a fresh install can inspect pending approvals but cannot\ndecide one until a human writes the policy down.\n\nCore policy denies financial, signature, employment, and destructive effect\nclasses outright; listing a principal here never overrides that.",
      "properties": {
        "authorized_principals": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "type": "array"
          },
          "title": "Authorized Principals",
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "title": "ApprovalsBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ArtifactConfig": {
      "description": "One project-supplied context artifact (a value in ``context.artifacts``).\n\n``path`` points at the audited, repository-tracked content the role reads;\n``sensitivity`` is the ceiling a selector must accept to receive it. The\nstring values mirror ``fno.roles.models.Sensitivity`` verbatim but are kept\nas a Literal here so the config layer never imports the roles package\n(roles imports paths, which imports config - that direction would cycle).",
      "properties": {
        "path": {
          "title": "Path",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "sensitivity": {
          "default": "internal",
          "enum": [
            "public",
            "internal",
            "sensitive",
            "restricted"
          ],
          "title": "Sensitivity",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "path"
      ],
      "title": "ArtifactConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AttentionBlock": {
      "description": "``sinks`` rows stay raw tables: the daemon checks each one and names a refusal.",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "sinks": {
          "items": {
            "additionalProperties": true,
            "type": "object"
          },
          "title": "Sinks",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "title": "AttentionBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AutoContinueBlock": {
      "description": "Merge-triggered auto-continue settings (nested under 'config.auto_continue').\n\nThe opt-in for merge-triggered auto-continue (node): when\nenabled, a merge-detector (``fno backlog reconcile`` / the /fno:ship pr merged skill)\ndispatches a fresh background ``/target --no-merge`` worker for the next\nnow-unblocked backlog node after a PR merges, so a merge-gated epic walks\nitself group-by-group with no manual re-invocation.\n\nDefault ``False`` (Locked Decision 3): shipping this changes nothing until\nthe operator arms it. Precedence mirrors ``config.auto_merge``: a malformed\nblock degrades to disabled (fail-safe) rather than failing the settings\nload, so one operator typo can never break every CLI invocation. The\nenable-resolution chain (env override > campaign-arm marker > this block)\nlives in :func:`fno.backlog.advance.auto_continue_enabled`.",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "AutoContinueBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AutoHealBlock": {
      "description": "The pr-watch tick's heal phase (nested under 'auto_heal').\n\n``enabled`` arms the phase that runs the CI heal drive loop\n(``fno do pr heal --all --apply`` in Rust) once per tick. Default false\nuntil the loop is measured on real PRs: an arm that pushes to branches\nis opt-in by design, like every other acting phase on the tick.",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "AutoHealBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AutoMergeBlock": {
      "description": "Auto-merge settings (nested under 'config.auto_merge').\n\nThe typed reader for what the bash ``scripts/lib/config.sh`` auto_merge\nhelpers used to parse (``is_auto_merge_allowed_for`` / ``get_auto_merge_*``).\nThe ``fno do pr`` port reads these via :func:`load_settings`\ninstead of re-parsing settings.yaml in a subprocess, so the 4-tier\nprecedence + caching live in one place.\n\nValidation mirrors the bash exactly: an invalid ``merge_strategy`` falls\nback to ``merge``, an invalid ``conflict_resolution`` to ``opus``, an\ninvalid ``remediation`` to ``attempt`` (the bash printed a warning and used\nthe same fallback). A malformed block degrades to defaults (auto-merge OFF)\nrather than failing the whole settings load - false-enabled is the dangerous\ndirection for a merge opt-in.\n\nScope-ordered to read like the AND chain ``fno do pr merge`` enforces:\n``enabled`` is PROJECT scope (the standing arm, re-read live at merge and\narm time so an operator disarm mid-flight still withholds);\n``grant`` is ACTOR scope (who may merge once ``enabled`` passes); the\npolicy keys below only matter once both do.\n\nRUN scope is deliberately not a key here. ``fno do target init`` folds\n``enabled`` plus ``grant`` plus ``--allow-merge`` / ``--no-merge`` plus the\n``/target bg`` injected default into ``auto_merge_approved`` in\n``.fno/target-state.md``, with ``auto_merge_source`` naming the decider.\nThe fold withholds and it grants: a per-run refusal (``false``) outranks\nevery grant at the merge gate (``pr/_merge.py``), and a\n``TARGET_AUTO_MERGE=1`` grant (``env-target-auto-merge``) satisfies the\nstanding arm on its own. Scrubbed on runs carrying a mesh\nidentity (``FNO_AGENT_SELF``) or an unattended marker; an interactive\nsession the operator launched carries neither and is the documented\ncarrier of the grant, inside the operator's trust boundary, with the\nsource stamp keeping every grant auditable.\nThe review rung of the same chain is ``config.review.required_bots`` /\n``config.review.reviewers``, enforced at the coverage guard in\n``_merge.py``.",
      "properties": {
        "conflict_resolution": {
          "default": "opus",
          "title": "Conflict Resolution",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "delete_branch_on_merge": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Delete Branch On Merge",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "grant": {
          "default": "none",
          "title": "Grant",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "merge_strategy": {
          "default": "merge",
          "title": "Merge Strategy",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "remediation": {
          "default": "attempt",
          "title": "Remediation",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "require_checks_pass": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Require Checks Pass",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "require_fresh_ci": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Require Fresh Ci",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "AutoMergeBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AutonomyBlock": {
      "description": "The one master switch over every autonomous session-starting spawner\n(nested under 'config.autonomy'). wave 3.\n\n``enabled=False`` stops EVERY spawner - the merge-triggered ones\n(advance, dispatch_lanes, epic converge, reconcile_dispatch), spawn_think,\npost-merge ritual, pr_watch, keep_going, and the\nwave-2 ones (groom, restart, evals) - regardless of that spawner's own\ngate. It is checked BEFORE any other precedence rank, even an explicit env\noverride: the whole point of a panic switch is that nothing overrides it.\nA skip caused by this switch stamps rank ``\"autonomy\"`` on its decision\nevent (distinct from env/config/default) so the log names the master\nswitch as the reason, never leaving it to inference (AC4-HP).\n\nDefault ``True``: shipping this changes nothing for an existing user -\nevery spawner's own gate still governs exactly as before until an\noperator explicitly arms the panic switch.\n\nExplicitly NOT a per-dispatcher lever (Alternative A in the design doc,\nrejected): nine levers multiply the state an operator must hold and\nguarantee some subset goes stale, which is the same failure with more\nsurface. This is the ONE switch; detail belongs in ``fno agents autonomy\nstatus``, not in a second layer of configuration.",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "AutonomyBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "BacklogBlock": {
      "description": "Backlog hygiene settings (nested under 'config.backlog').\n\n``id_prefix`` / ``id_hex_width`` configure the node-ID minting scheme\n(``<prefix><hex>``). Schema defaults are the LEGACY values - an absent\n``id_prefix`` (``None``) falls back to ``ab-`` at the accessor, and the width\ndefaults to 8 - so an existing ``config.backlog`` block with no id keys is\nbyte-identical. The setup wizard OFFERS width 4 for new installs; that is the\nwizard's default, not the schema default (AC3-FR).",
      "properties": {
        "epic_max_open_children": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "minimum": 1,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Epic Max Open Children"
        },
        "id_hex_width": {
          "default": 8,
          "title": "Id Hex Width",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "id_prefix": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Id Prefix"
        },
        "maintain": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/MaintainBlock"
        },
        "max_open_ideas": {
          "default": 25,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Max Open Ideas",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "page_reload_s": {
          "default": 60,
          "title": "Page Reload S",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "render_targets": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/RenderTargetConfig"
          },
          "title": "Render Targets",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "staleness_days": {
          "default": 21,
          "title": "Staleness Days",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "title": "BacklogBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "BatchBlock": {
      "description": "Batch-lane settings (nested under 'config.batch').\n\nThe auto-target runner can coalesce N same-domain ready nodes onto one\nbranch and open ONE PR per batch instead of one-per-node, cutting GitHub\nActions runs ~N\u00d7 (the cost driver is PR *volume*, not bad merges).\n\nDefault OFF (footnote opt-in convention): with `enabled=false` the selection\npath is byte-for-byte today's one-PR-per-node behavior. A malformed\n`enabled` fails safe to disabled (mirrors config.auto_merge / cross_model) \u2014\nfalse-enabled is the dangerous direction because a bad batch could pool\nunrelated work into one PR.\n\nKnobs:\n  enabled   - whole-feature opt-in.\n  max_nodes - nodes per batch before it closes (domain boundary + size/p0\n              can close it sooner). Non-positive/malformed \u2192 default 3.\n  max_loc   - optional cumulative-diff LOC ceiling (None = off).",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "max_loc": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Max Loc"
        },
        "max_nodes": {
          "default": 3,
          "title": "Max Nodes",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "title": "BatchBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "BlastConfig": {
      "description": "Blast-radius router settings (nested under 'config.target.blast').\n\nA deterministic blast read at `/target` init modulates the size profile\nBEFORE the immutable manifest is written: a high-blast surface can only\nraise ceremony (a non-overridable floor at `M`), and low-blast work is\ndowngraded to the fast path only when the operator did not pin a size.\n\nDefault OFF (footnote convention): disabled is byte-for-byte today's\nbehavior. A malformed block fails safe to disabled, mirroring\n`config.auto_merge` / `config.auto_continue`; a single bad glob in\n`high_blast_globs` is skipped, not raised (the classifier owns that).\n\nKnobs:\n  enabled          - whole-feature opt-in.\n  downgrade        - when False, only the high-blast floor applies\n                     (safety-only mode; no token-saving downgrades).\n  reuse_loc_manifest - legacy key spelling; include the packaged\n                     control-plane scope in the map.\n  high_blast_globs - per-project extension of the general default list.",
      "properties": {
        "downgrade": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Downgrade",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "high_blast_globs": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "High Blast Globs",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "reuse_loc_manifest": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Reuse Loc Manifest",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "BlastConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "BlueprintBlock": {
      "description": "Blueprint / epic-decomposition settings (nested under 'config.blueprint').",
      "properties": {
        "max_prs_per_epic": {
          "default": 4,
          "title": "Max Prs Per Epic",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "python_repair_added_lines": {
          "default": 30,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Python Repair Added Lines",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "title": "BlueprintBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "BranchBlock": {
      "description": "Dispatch branch naming (nested under 'config.branch', W3).\n\n``prefix`` is the leading segment of a dispatched worktree branch:\n``<prefix>/<slug>-<node>`` (e.g. ``fno/plan-docs-...-x-aaaa``). A legible\nbranch that round-trips back to its node beats the opaque ``feature/<hex>``.",
      "properties": {
        "prefix": {
          "default": "fno",
          "title": "Prefix",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "title": "BranchBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "BuildBlock": {
      "description": "Build-freeze switch (nested under 'config.build').",
      "properties": {
        "agent_freeze": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Agent Freeze",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "BuildBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "CodexAgentBlock": {
      "description": "The codex block: the provider settings plus its lead beat.",
      "properties": {
        "beat": {
          "default": "auto",
          "title": "Beat",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "headless_yolo": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Headless Yolo",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "CodexAgentBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "CollisionBlock": {
      "description": "File-collision detection settings (config.collision).",
      "properties": {
        "severity_thresholds": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/CollisionThresholdsBlock"
        }
      },
      "title": "CollisionBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "CollisionThresholdsBlock": {
      "description": "Collision severity scoring thresholds (config.collision.severity_thresholds).\n\nDefaults lifted verbatim from the collision module's original private\nloader; the native thresholds reader holds the same contract.",
      "properties": {
        "high_count": {
          "default": 3,
          "title": "High Count",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "high_ratio": {
          "default": 0.5,
          "title": "High Ratio",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "medium_count": {
          "default": 2,
          "title": "Medium Count",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "medium_ratio": {
          "default": 0.25,
          "title": "Medium Ratio",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "title": "CollisionThresholdsBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ComboBlock": {
      "description": "Named combo specification (nested under 'config.accounts.combos.<name>').",
      "properties": {
        "providers": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Providers",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "sticky_limit": {
          "default": 1,
          "title": "Sticky Limit",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "strategy": {
          "default": "fallback",
          "enum": [
            "fallback",
            "round_robin"
          ],
          "title": "Strategy",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "title": "ComboBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ContextBlock": {
      "description": "Project-supplied context artifacts (nested under 'config.context').\n\nA GENERIC identifier -> artifact map. Core never learns a function's\nvocabulary: a role's context selector names an identifier and the\ninstalling project resolves it here, so a pack installed in a second\nproject is reviewed against that project's facts, not the first's. Empty\nby default; an unconfigured identifier blocks resolution with\nMISSING_CONTEXT rather than falling back to a pack asset.",
      "properties": {
        "artifacts": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/ArtifactConfig"
          },
          "title": "Artifacts",
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "title": "ContextBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "CrossModelBlock": {
      "description": "Cross-model review opt-in (nested under 'config.review.cross_model').\n\nGates the diversity axis of review (; the sigma panel it once\nrouted is removed): when `enabled` is true, reviewer capacity\nmay include a different provider (codex/gemini) than wrote the code,\ncatching model-specific blind spots - the peer rung's substrate and the\nassurance resolver's effective kinds. Default False: existing all-claude\nreview is byte-for-byte unchanged until the operator turns it on (Locked\nDecision 7). An explicit `config.review.agent_providers` map ALSO engages\ncross-model (the selector treats either signal as opt-in); this flag is\nthe no-map-needed switch.",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "CrossModelBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "DevBlock": {
      "description": "Maintainer local-dev settings (nested under 'config.dev').\n\n``source`` is the machine-local pin the Rust bootstrap reads to re-provision\nfrom a checkout instead of the published PyPI wheel when its uv tool venv is\nwiped. Unset (the default) keeps the frictionless PyPI self-provision\nfor end users; a maintainer sets it to their checkout root to make recovery\nsource-first, matching the repo's \"unset = OSS-neutral, set = maintainer\nchoice\" pattern (``paths.worktrees_base``).\n\nThe bootstrap reads this key from ``~/.fno/config.toml`` DIRECTLY (fno-free:\nit runs precisely because ``fno`` is broken). The read is hard-coded in\n``crates/fno/src/bootstrap.rs::parse_dev_source`` as ``[dev].source``; the\ncross-language test in ``cli/tests/unit/test_dev_source_pin.py`` pins the two\nsides so a rename here can't silently break recovery.",
      "properties": {
        "source": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Source",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "title": "DevBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "DifficultyLaneBlock": {
      "description": "One difficulty rung of ``profiles.<command>.by_difficulty``.\n\nMirrors exactly what the Rust route-slot reader accepts inside an entry\n(crates/fno-agents/src/route_slot.rs:903: lanes plus the three policy\nleaves, nothing else). Any change to either side must move both.",
      "properties": {
        "lanes": {
          "title": "Lanes"
        },
        "on_exhausted": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "On Exhausted",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "on_low": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "On Low",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "on_unknown": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "On Unknown",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "title": "DifficultyLaneBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "DispatchBlock": {
      "description": "Autonomous-dispatch profile (nested under 'config.dispatch').\n\nPer-environment overlay of the in-tree harness-capability map\n(`fno.agents.harness_map`): the shared `resolve_node_spawn` resolver reads\nthese as the config rung between an explicit flag and the built-in default.\nAll three are empty (\"\") = unset, so a fresh install resolves exactly as the\nbuilt-ins (harness=claude, per-harness substrate, `/target --no-merge {id}`).\n\nNo value validation here: the resolver checks harness and substrate at\nresolve time, fail-loud.\n\n`command` is a template with a single `{id}` placeholder. A node's\n`dispatch_command`/`dispatch_brief` (US3) layer on top: the resolver validates\nthe command against `allowed_commands` and carries the brief via env only, so a\ngraph field crossing into a worker prompt is a guarded trust boundary.",
      "properties": {
        "allowed_commands": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Allowed Commands",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "auto_merge": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Auto Merge",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "blueprint_floor": {
          "default": "high",
          "title": "Blueprint Floor",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "command": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Command",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "command_registry": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/DispatchCommandDescriptor"
          },
          "title": "Command Registry",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "cutover_low_after_minutes": {
          "default": 0,
          "title": "Cutover Low After Minutes",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "harness": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Harness",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "on_exhaustion": {
          "default": "defer",
          "title": "On Exhaustion",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "substrate": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Substrate",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "title": "DispatchBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "DispatchCommandDescriptor": {
      "properties": {
        "asserts": {
          "default": "invocation",
          "enum": [
            "pr",
            "doc",
            "invocation"
          ],
          "title": "Asserts",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "invocation": {
          "title": "Invocation",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "invocations": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "additionalProperties": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Invocations"
        },
        "requires": {
          "default": "none",
          "enum": [
            "none",
            "skill"
          ],
          "title": "Requires",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "session_phase": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Session Phase"
        },
        "takes_node_id": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Takes Node Id",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "invocation"
      ],
      "title": "DispatchCommandDescriptor",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "EvalsBlock": {
      "description": "Eval-suite settings: the grading-worker gate plus the demand keys.\nFull key docs live in the generated reference and docs/evals.md.",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": true,
