        }
      },
      "title": "ProjectBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ProviderBudget": {
      "description": "What ONE account at a model provider tolerates, in every dimension.\n\nThe fleet already had a per-provider record: `agents.provider_limits.<provider>` (then `max_lanes`),\na bare integer capping concurrent spawned workers. It carried one dimension\nwhile the account is spent on two - a worker also fans out subagents inside\nits own session, and a shared-quota account was spent eight subagents deep\non one review that returned nothing.\n\n`subagents` is that second dimension, and it is consumed by ROUTE\nRESOLUTION rather than by a guard: a native subagent is a harness-internal\nTask call fno never observes, so a spawn-path guard is decorative for\nexactly the case that cost the account. The capability resolver that once\nread this budget to refuse a panel reviewer is gone (the native\n`review-level capability` door replaced it); a worker cannot fan out a\npanel it was never handed.\n\n`None` on either field means unbounded in that dimension, which is what an\nunlisted provider gets: today's behavior for every dedicated account.",
      "properties": {
        "lanes": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Lanes"
        },
        "subagents": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Subagents"
        }
      },
      "title": "ProviderBudget",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "QuotaBlock": {
      "description": "Quota-aware dispatch configuration (nested under 'config.accounts.quota').\n\n``observe`` and ``defer_dispatch`` are two decisions, not one: looking at\nquota and acting on it. ``defer_dispatch`` implies ``observe``.",
      "properties": {
        "defer_dispatch": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Defer Dispatch",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "defer_horizon_minutes": {
          "default": 60,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Defer Horizon Minutes",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "defer_threshold_pct": {
          "default": 90.0,
          "maximum": 100.0,
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Defer Threshold Pct",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "observe": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Observe",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "pick_on_launch": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Pick On Launch",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "probe_ttl_seconds": {
          "default": 300,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Probe Ttl Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "title": "QuotaBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ReapBlock": {
      "description": "Scope of the roster-side sweep (nested under 'config.agents.reap').\n\n``roster_scope`` names which claude rows the sweep may retire:\n``off`` retires nothing, ``provenanced`` (the default) only rows whose\nprovenance resolves to fno and whose work is done, ``all`` widens to\nrows fno itself spawned (sessions or registry provenance) with open\nwork. One rule no value can cross: a row that resolves to no fno node\nis never retirable at any value, including ``all`` - an operator's\nhand-started session is safe by construction, not by default value.",
      "properties": {
        "roster_scope": {
          "default": "provenanced",
          "title": "Roster Scope",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "title": "ReapBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ReapReceiptsBlock": {
      "description": "Retention for readable, aged reap receipts under ``config.agents``.",
      "properties": {
        "retain_days": {
          "default": 7,
          "title": "Retain Days",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "title": "ReapReceiptsBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "RecoveryBlock": {
      "description": "Bg-session recovery sweep settings (nested under 'config.recovery').\n\nControls the Layer-2 sweep that rides the ``pr_watch`` launchd\ntick over footnote-launched bg sessions. Two actions survive the\nremoval of the held socket nudge: provider failover on a swap-class death\n(rate-limit / quota / auth / 5xx; respawns a fresh ``claude --bg``), and\nclose-surfacing for a session whose mission finished but whose process\nstill lingers. It only runs when ``pr_watch`` is installed (it shares that\ncadence) AND ``enabled`` here is true; even then it is a no-op unless an\nidle-stale footnote bg session exists.\n\nFields\n------\nenabled:\n    True to run the recovery sweep each pr_watch tick (default True; the\n    target audience for pr_watch is exactly bg-session operators). Set\n    false to keep pr_watch's PR polling without the recovery sweep.\nidle_threshold_seconds:\n    How old family-1 transcript activity may be before recovery acts on a\n    session (default 900 = 15 min). Keep it above the longest expected\n    single-tool runtime: a long build legitimately produces no turn.\nmax_nudges:\n    Per-session cap on held-by-design surfaces before the sweep gives up\n    and emits ``recovery_capped`` (default 3). Close notifications are\n    once-only, tracked separately.\nwatchdog:\n    The fleet watchdog lane, as a nested block. See\n    :mod:`fno.config._watchdog`.",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "idle_threshold_seconds": {
          "default": 900,
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
          "title": "Idle Threshold Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "max_nudges": {
          "default": 3,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Max Nudges",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "provider_health_marker_ttl_seconds": {
          "default": 120,
          "minimum": 120,
          "title": "Provider Health Marker Ttl Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "provider_outage_529_count": {
          "default": 3,
          "minimum": 3,
          "title": "Provider Outage 529 Count",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "provider_outage_529_cross_session_window_seconds": {
          "default": 600,
          "minimum": 600,
          "title": "Provider Outage 529 Cross Session Window Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "provider_outage_529_span_seconds": {
          "default": 120,
          "minimum": 120,
          "title": "Provider Outage 529 Span Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "provider_outage_evidence_freshness_seconds": {
          "default": 600,
          "minimum": 600,
          "title": "Provider Outage Evidence Freshness Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "provider_outage_fup_window_seconds": {
          "default": 300,
          "minimum": 300,
          "title": "Provider Outage Fup Window Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "provider_outage_pane_freshness_seconds": {
          "default": 120,
          "minimum": 120,
          "title": "Provider Outage Pane Freshness Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "provider_outage_quorum": {
          "default": 2,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Provider Outage Quorum",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "provider_outage_reset_grace_seconds": {
          "default": 120,
          "minimum": 120,
          "title": "Provider Outage Reset Grace Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "startup_destructive": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Startup Destructive",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "watchdog": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/WatchdogBlock"
        }
      },
      "title": "RecoveryBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "RenderTargetConfig": {
      "description": "One auto-rendered backlog projection (``config.backlog.render_targets[]``).\n\n``local`` (the default) renders the unified board page; ``backlog`` and\n``roadmap`` name retired public HTML projections and warn-skip. ``scope``\nnames one project or ``all``. ``project`` remains accepted as a\ncompatibility spelling.",
      "properties": {
        "path": {
          "title": "Path",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "project": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Project"
        },
        "projection": {
          "default": "local",
          "title": "Projection",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "scope": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Scope"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "path"
      ],
      "title": "RenderTargetConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ResearchBlock": {
      "description": "`fno do research` doc-deliverable settings (nested under 'config.research').\n\n`output_dir` is the landing area for the research `doc` deliverable: the\nbrief (`<slug>.md`) and its evidence sidecar (`<slug>.sources.jsonl`) are\nwritten there. Unlike `post_merge.parking_lot_path` this is NOT repo-relative\n- it is a vault/output area (e.g. ~/c3po/raw/readyrule), so absolute and\n'~'-anchored paths are allowed. Left unset by default so a repo that has not\nopted in fails loud at the ship step rather than guessing a landing path\n(the parking_lot_path lesson, AC5).",
      "properties": {
        "output_dir": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Output Dir"
        }
      },
      "title": "ResearchBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ResourceMeterBlock": {
      "description": "The whole-machine resource meter (config.resource_meter).\n\nSame four parts as ``config.health_monitor``: an enable, thresholds, a\nnotification routing block, and a history block. ``enabled`` defaults to\nFALSE - the feature needs the ``macmon`` binary on PATH, which fno core\ndoes not depend on, and a meter that silently renders nothing on a machine\nwithout it must not be on by default. This is a plain feature toggle by\noperator ruling: no adapter interface, no plugin registry, no\ndiscriminator.",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "history": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/HealthHistoryBlock"
        },
        "notifications": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/HealthNotificationsBlock"
        },
        "refresh_seconds": {
          "default": 5,
          "title": "Refresh Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "thresholds": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ResourceMeterThresholdsBlock"
        }
      },
      "title": "ResourceMeterBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ResourceMeterThresholdsBlock": {
      "description": "Whole-machine resource thresholds the meter may flag against.\n\n``swap_used_gb``: swap in use above this reads as memory pressure. It is\nadvisory for now - the meter renders readings, it gates nothing yet - but\nthe shape is here so a later gate does not re-derive the numbers.",
      "properties": {
        "cpu_busy_fraction": {
          "default": 0.9,
          "title": "Cpu Busy Fraction",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "swap_used_gb": {
          "default": 1.0,
          "title": "Swap Used Gb",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "title": "ResourceMeterThresholdsBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ReviewBlock": {
      "description": "External-review gate settings (nested under 'config.review').\n\n    `github_apps` is the must-have-reviewed list of GitHub App bot logins\n    consumed by the `fno-agents loop-check` review gate (control-plane step 2,\n): a session terminates DonePRGreen only when every listed login\n    has at least one completed review pass and no unaddressed blocking finding.\n\n    Semantics (mirrors the Rust-side parser in loopcheck.rs):\n      - key absent (None)  -> no review gate (PR + CI only); a fresh install\n                              completes without hanging on a bot it never set up.\n                              The effective Rust default is [] (cv-6537099f); the\n                              old [\"chatgpt-codex-connector\"] docstring was wrong.\n      - explicit []        -> declared no-review-gate path (PR + CI only),\n                              mirroring ci.declared_none; never auto-detected\n      - non-empty list     -> every listed login must pass\n\n    `peers` are harness peers (codex/gemini/...) run locally. Identity-free\n    entries satisfy one composite, head-pinned local-attestation gate when any\n    configured cross-model peer returns a clean verdict. An explicit entry\n    `identity` or shared `peer_identity` retains the legacy mode that posts a\n    GitHub review and gates on that login.\n\n    `required_bots` is a legacy alias for `github_apps` (a straight rename).\n    Existing configs are unchanged; if both are set, `github_apps` wins.\n\n    Distinct from `config.external_reviewers` (the recognition/matching\n    list): that list says which logins count as bots; `github_apps` says which\n    logins are REQUIRED to have reviewed.\n    ",
      "properties": {
        "agent_harnesses": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Agent Harnesses",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "agent_providers": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Agent Providers",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "agent_routes": {
          "additionalProperties": true,
          "title": "Agent Routes",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "bot_identity": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Bot Identity"
        },
        "bot_token_env": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Bot Token Env"
        },
        "carry_interdiff_lines": {
          "default": 100,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Carry Interdiff Lines",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "cross_model": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/CrossModelBlock"
        },
        "external_reviewers": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "External Reviewers",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "github_approval_satisfies": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Github Approval Satisfies",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "github_apps": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Github Apps"
        },
        "hold_ttl_minutes": {
          "default": 90,
          "title": "Hold Ttl Minutes",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "invocation_ttl_minutes": {
          "default": 15,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Invocation Ttl Minutes",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "max_rounds": {
          "default": 2,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Max Rounds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "nonblocking_categories": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Nonblocking Categories"
        },
        "nudge": {
          "additionalProperties": true,
          "title": "Nudge",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "optional_apps": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Optional Apps"
        },
        "optout_ttl_minutes": {
          "default": 60,
          "maximum": 1440,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Optout Ttl Minutes",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "peer_identity": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Peer Identity"
        },
        "peer_token_env": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Peer Token Env"
        },
        "peers": {
          "items": {},
          "title": "Peers",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "posture": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Posture"
        },
        "require_corroboration": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Require Corroboration",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "required_bots": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Required Bots"
        },
        "reviewer_registry": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/ReviewerDescriptor"
          },
          "title": "Reviewer Registry",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "reviewers": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Reviewers",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "self_review_required": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Self Review Required",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "ReviewBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ReviewerDescriptor": {
      "description": "What a `config.review.reviewers` entry needs in order to actually run.\n\nA name alone cannot answer \"can this reviewer run unattended, here?\" - the\nquestion that made a `reviewers: [sigma]` gate unsatisfiable-by-construction\non a harness with no subagent dispatch, discovered only after the work was\ndone. These four fields are what the init capability check and the\nloop-check blocked reason both render from, so neither can invent its own\nstory about a reviewer.",
      "properties": {
        "asserts": {
          "enum": [
            "review-evidence",
            "self-cert",
            "invocation"
          ],
          "title": "Asserts",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "invocation": {
          "title": "Invocation",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "invocations": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "additionalProperties": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Invocations"
        },
        "kind": {
          "enum": [
            "local-attestation",
            "github-app",
            "external-cli",
            "human",
            "harness-skill"
          ],
          "title": "Kind",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "requires": {
          "enum": [
            "none",
            "subagent-dispatch",
            "operator",
            "skill",
            "retired"
          ],
          "title": "Requires",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "kind",
        "requires",
        "invocation",
        "asserts"
      ],
      "title": "ReviewerDescriptor",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "RoutingBlock": {
      "description": "Config-first model routing inventory (nested under 'config.routing').\n\nConfig overrides the built-in fallback table per model and per field and\nextends it; the fallback only keeps a tier request answerable where\nnothing is declared. Full policy: docs/architecture/role-based-model-routing.md.",
      "properties": {
        "enforce_inventory": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enforce Inventory",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "models": {
          "items": {
            "additionalProperties": true,
            "type": "object"
          },
          "title": "Models",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "objective": {
          "default": "cheapest-that-clears",
          "title": "Objective",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "operator_access": {
          "default": "unknown",
          "title": "Operator Access",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "prefer_harness": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Prefer Harness",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "title": "RoutingBlock",
      "type": "object"
    },
